#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:178
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "\"Flake\" is not a root cause. A red PR is work now, whatever its review state — only a green, mergeable head waits on reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:215
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`prepare-merge` brings the base in, re-runs the gates and pushes — it does NOT merge. `watch` follows the PR until it is merged or closed, because webhooks do not reliably deliver CI success or a merge-conflict transition."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:229
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A closed work item is read later by somebody deciding whether to reopen the subject, so \"completed\" with nothing behind it cannot be audited. An ISSUE is never closed on the agent's own say-so."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:264
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A human or an agent acting AS reviewer. Nothing is a reviewer; somebody acts as one for the duration of this lane."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:93
#. Diagram label
msgid "A platform change is needed"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:195
#. Diagram label
msgid "Address the review"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:112
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Announce the branch WHEN IT IS CREATED, not when the work is done. The gap between one agent's view of an issue and everyone else's is what this closes."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:55
#. Diagram label
msgid "Authoring agent"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:139
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Before pushing, not after CI says so. `bun test` passing is NOT the gates passing: measured 2026-09-19, a green unit suite sat beside a `tsc` failure and a missing `@graphNode` tag, and the second broke a QA sidecar comparison as well — one cause, two symptoms, and an agent running only the tests would have pushed all three."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:111
#. Diagram label
msgid "Branch, and announce it"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:171
#. Diagram label
msgid "CI green?"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:249
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "CI tests the MERGE, not the branch. That is why a locally green tree can go red here: the agent's tree and the merge result are different trees, and the difference is invisible from a checkout."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:78
#. Diagram label
msgid "CI/CD pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/code-change-review.bpmn:98
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Claim before you work. A claim ANNOUNCES rather than reserves until the PR exists, which is why the branch is announced at the next step and not at the end."
msgstr ""

